h token attends only to a fixed-size window of </span><em>t</em><span> rece=
nt tokens (for example, 4096) instead of attending to the entire input (whi=
ch could be up to </span><em>n=3D256,000</em><span> tokens). This reduces t=
he per-layer regular attention cost from O(</span><em>n</em><span>=C2=B2) t=
o roughly O(</span><em>n</em><span>=C2=B7</span><em>t</em><span>) for seque=
nce length </span><em>n</em><span>, which is why it is attractive for long-=
