hat Gemma 3 and Xiaomi used, the Arcee team opted for a 3:1 ratio similar t=
o Olmo 3, and a relatively large sliding window size of 4096 (also similar =
to Olmo 3).</p><p><span>The architecture also uses </span><a href=3D"https:=
//magazine.sebastianraschka.com/i/168650848/22-qk-norm">QK-Norm</a><span>, =
which is a technique that applies RMSNorm to the keys and queries to stabil=
ize training (as shown in Figure 4 below), as well as no positional embeddi=
ngs (</span><a href=3D"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/i/168650848/71=
-no-positional-embeddings-nope">NoPE</a><span>) in the global attention lay=
ers similar to </span><a href=3D"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/i/16=
8650848/7-smollm3">SmolLM3</a><span>.</span></p><p><span>Trinity also has a=
 form of gated attention. It=E2=80=99s not a full-blown </span><a href=3D"h=
ttps://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/i/168650848/122-gated-deltanet-gated-a=
ttention-hybrid">Gated DeltaNet</a><span> but it uses a similar gating as i=
n the attention mechanism in </span><a href=3D"https://magazine.sebastianra=
schka.com/i/168650848/6-qwen3">Qwen3-Next</a><span>.</span></p><p><span>I.e=
., the Trinity team modified the standard attention by adding elementwise g=
ating to the scaled dot-product before the output linear projection (as sho=
wn in the figure below), which reduces </span><a href=3D"https://magazine.s=
ebastianraschka.com/i/168650848/93-attention-bias-and-attention-sinks">atte=
ntion sinks</a><span> and improves long-sequence generalization. Additional=
ly, it also helped with training stability.</span></p><div class=3D"caption=
