/div></a><figcaption class=3D"image-caption"><em>Figure 17: The Qwen3-Coder=
-Next attention hybrid setup.</em></figcaption></figure></div><p>We can thi=
nk of the gated attention block as standard scaled-dot-product attention us=
ed in GQA, with a few tweaks on top. The main differences between gated att=
ention and plain GQA block are:</p><ol><li><p>an output gate (sigmoid-contr=
olled, usually per-channel) that scales the attention result before it is a=
dded back to the residual;</p></li><li><p>zero-centered RMSNorm for QKNorm,=
 rather than a standard RMSNorm;</p></li><li><p>partial RoPE (on a subset o=
f dimensions).</p></li></ol><p>Note that these are essentially just stabili=
ty changes to GQA.</p><p><span>The Gated DeltaNet is a more significant cha=
nge. In the DeltaNet block, q, k, v, and two gates (=CE=B1, =CE=B2) are pro=
duced by linear and lightweight convolutional layers with normalization, an=
d the layer replaces attention with a fast=E2=80=91weight</span><a href=3D"=
https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.06464"> delta rule</a><span> update.</span></p><=
p>However, the tradeoff is that DeltaNet offers less precise content=E2=80=
=91based retrieval than full attention, which is why one gated attention la=
yer remains.</p><p>Given that attention grows quadratically, the DeltaNet c=
omponent was added to help with memory efficiency. In the =E2=80=9Clinear-t=
ime, cache-free=E2=80=9D family, the DeltaNet block is essentially an alter=
native to Mamba. Mamba keeps a state with a learned state-space filter (ess=
entially a dynamic convolution over time). DeltaNet keeps a tiny, fast-weig=
ht memory updated with =CE=B1 and =CE=B2, and reads it with q, using small =
convolutions only to help form q, k, v, =CE=B1, =CE=B2.</p><p><span>For mor=
e details on the attention hybrid and Qwen3-Next architecture, please see m=
y previous article</span><a href=3D"https://magazine.sebastianraschka.com/i=
/177848019/24-qwen3-next"> Beyond Standard LLMs</a><span>.</span></p><p><sp=
an>=E2=80=8BSince this article is primarily focused on LLM architectures, t=
he training details are outside its scope. However, interested readers can =
find more information in their detailed</span><a href=3D"https://github.com=
/QwenLM/Qwen3-Coder/blob/main/qwen3_coder_next_tech_report.pdf"> technical =
report on GitHub.</a></p><h1 class=3D"header-anchor-post">5. z.AI=E2=80=99s=
